---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="The Jentosy Project's mission, vision, and why our focus shifted from transplantation toward kidney disease education and health equity."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About The Jentosy Project"
    heading="Health equity, treated as inseparable from the systems that produce disease."
  />

  <section class="on-light section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Mission</p>
        <p class="pull">
          The Jentosy Project advances health equity for underserved communities by educating
          people about rare kidney diseases — including FSGS, APOL1-mediated kidney disease, and
          IgA Nephropathy — and building the partnerships needed to close the gap in kidney care.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:var(--space-8);">
        <p class="eyebrow">Vision</p>
        <p class="pull" style="border-left-color:var(--steel);">
          A future where no one's zip code determines their access to kidney health education,
          early detection, or life-saving care — starting in the Bronx and expanding to
          underserved communities nationwide.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="on-light section-tight" style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="h2">Why our focus is education, not just transplantation.</h2>
      <p>
        The Jentosy Project's work began with transplantation — but the deeper problem is
        upstream: too many people from underserved communities are diagnosed too late, or never
        learn they're at risk, for diseases like FSGS, APOL1-mediated kidney disease, and IgA
        Nephropathy. That's why our current focus is education and health equity — reaching
        people before they reach the transplant list. Transplantation equity remains part of our
        long-term mission, and it's where we're headed next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="on-light section-tight" style="border-top:1px solid var(--line);">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="h2">Kidney disease doesn't happen in isolation.</h2>
      <p>
        Kidney disease disparities are downstream of poverty, unequal access to education,
        incarceration, broken homes, and the chronic stress those conditions produce — all of
        which take a measurable toll on the body, including the kidneys. The Jentosy Project
        treats health equity as inseparable from these upstream social conditions, not just a
        matter of medical access.
      </p>
      <p>
        We start in the Bronx, where these conditions are concentrated and where our founder's
        own story began — and we intend to expand as the organization grows.
        <a href="/founders-story/">Read the founder's story &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
</style>
